---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="SF Ruby News - June 2026"
    description="June 2026 edition of SF Ruby News: Salesforce acquires Fin (formerly Intercom) for $3.6B, all on a 2M-line Rails monolith. The SF Ruby Startup Conference is announced for SFJAZZ with keynote Garry Tan. 1Password acquires Apono. Factorial raises $150M at $2.5B. Clio crosses $500M ARR. RubyConf 2026 heads to Las Vegas."
>
    <section class="relative px-night text-white overflow-hidden min-h-screen">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 pt-32 pb-16">

            <!-- Issue Navigation -->
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8 text-sm">
                <a href="/news/2026-05/" class="text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-1">
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
                    May 2026
                </a>
                <a href="/news/2026-07/" class="text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-1">
                    July 2026
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
                </a>
            </div>

            <!-- Masthead -->
            <div class="text-center mb-12">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 justify-center mb-3">
                    <div class="flex-1 max-w-[120px] h-1 bg-white/25"></div>
                    <a href="/#news" class="px-font text-base md:text-xl text-white hover:text-gold-400 transition-colors">SF Ruby News</a>
                    <div class="flex-1 max-w-[120px] h-1 bg-white/25"></div>
                </div>
                <p class="px-font text-[0.625rem] text-gold-400">June 2026</p>
            </div>

            <!-- News Carousel -->
            <div class="relative" id="news-carousel">

                <!-- Page 1 -->
                <div class="news-page" data-page="0">
                    <!-- Headline Story: Salesforce acquires Fin -->
                    <div class="mb-10">
                        <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-4">Acquisition</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Salesforce Acquires Fin for $3.6B</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-4 border-ruby-500 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                Salesforce signs a definitive agreement to buy <strong class="text-white">Fin</strong>, the AI customer-service company that was <strong class="text-white">Intercom</strong> until last month's rebrand, for roughly <strong class="text-white">$3.6 billion</strong>, the largest acquisition ever of an Irish-founded tech company. Fin's AI Agent runs on its purpose-built Apex model, all of it on Intercom's 2M-line Rails monolith.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                The deal lands a month after Intercom renamed itself Fin and crossed $100M ARR, growing 3.5x inside a $400M+ ARR business. It's Salesforce's fifth acquisition of 2026, joining M3ter and Contentful, and feeds an Agentforce business that reached $1.2B ARR last quarter. Expected to close in Q4 of Salesforce's fiscal 2027.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">June 15, 2026 · Salesforce</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://www.salesforce.com/news/press-releases/2026/06/15/salesforce-signs-definitive-agreement-to-acquire-fin/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Read the announcement
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-[2px] bg-white/15 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 (events) -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-10">
                        <!-- Conference: SF Ruby Startup Conference -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-3">Conference</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">SF Ruby Startup Conference Announced</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">November 10–12, 2026 · SFJAZZ</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Our first conference: three days at <strong class="text-white/80">SFJAZZ</strong> in San Francisco, keynoted by <strong class="text-white/80">Garry Tan</strong>, President &amp; CEO of Y Combinator. Tickets aren't on sale yet; sponsorships are open now.</p>
                            <a href="/conference-2026" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Conference details
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: RubyConf 2026 Las Vegas -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">RubyConf 2026 Heads to Las Vegas</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">July 14–16, 2026 · Red Rock Resort</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Ruby Central's flagship conference returns for three days of talks, live coding, and community in Las Vegas, welcoming everyone from newcomers to teams at global companies. The room block at Red Rock Resort closes June 19.</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyconf.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Register
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: SF Ruby Meetup -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">SF Ruby Meetup, June @ PlanetScale</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">June 18, 2026 · 108 Natoma St.</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Jeremy Evans on "Implementing Core Set," Alan Ridlehoover's "Indispensable: What Human Computers Can Teach Human Programmers," plus a PlanetScale talk and interest circles. Hosted with Sam Lambert. 108+ RSVPs.</p>
                            <a href="https://lu.ma/ltipgvuh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                RSVP on Luma
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 (business) -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit">Acquisition</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">1Password Acquires Apono</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The Rails Foundation Core member buys <strong class="text-white/80">Apono</strong>, a just-in-time access-governance platform for humans, machines, and AI agents (June 15). It extends 1Password from securing credentials to governing what every identity can reach, and for how long. Terms undisclosed.</p>
                                <a href="https://1password.com/press/2026/june/1password-acquires-apono" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit">Funding</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Factorial Raises $150M at $2.5B</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Barcelona's HR platform (Rails backend, 200+ product engineers) closes a $150M Series D led by General Catalyst, with up to $540M more through GC's Customer Value Fund (June 3). 16,000 businesses across 90 countries, ~2,600 employees, one of Europe's most valuable AI scale-ups.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/factorial-raises-150m-series-d-reaches-2-5-billion-valuation-to-become-one-of-the-most-valuable-ai-scale-ups-in-europe-302789074.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Clio Crosses $500M ARR</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The legal practice platform and longtime Rails shop hits $500M in annual recurring revenue, up from $400M six months prior, serving legal professionals in 130+ countries. CEO Jack Newton frames it as joining "a rare class of profitable, accelerating AI platforms." Follows the $1B vLex acquisition and a $5B valuation.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.clio.com/about/press/clio-500-million-arr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Hiring strip -->
                    <div class="mt-4 mb-6 border-2 border-gold-500/50 px-6 py-4 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-3 md:gap-6">
                        <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-gold-500 text-ink text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit shrink-0">Hiring</span>
                        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed flex-1">Fresh Ruby roles on the board, every listing re-verified this week: <strong class="text-white/80">Gusto</strong> (Staff, Payments/Risk), <strong class="text-white/80">Superconductor</strong> (Principal Rails), <strong class="text-white/80">Koah Labs</strong> (Backend, Product, Platform), <strong class="text-white/80">Omada Health</strong>, <strong class="text-white/80">CompanyCam</strong>, plus open roles at Thatch, Persona, Chime, Patch, Reset, and Finta.</p>
                        <a href="/jobs" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors shrink-0">
                            Browse all jobs
                            <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Page 2 -->
                <div class="news-page hidden" data-page="1">
                    <!-- Headline Story: RubyConf Austria -->
                    <div class="mb-10">
                        <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-4">Event</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">RubyConf Austria Draws the Legends to Vienna</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-4 border-ruby-500 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                <strong class="text-white">Dave Thomas</strong> opens with "Start Writing Ruby." <strong class="text-white">Chad Fowler</strong> answers with "This is What We've Been Training For." One panel seats Fowler, <strong class="text-white">José Valim</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Obie Fernandez</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">Armin Ronacher</strong> on the same stage.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                22 talks over three days: Bozhidar Batsov asks "RuboCop 2.0: Where do we go now?", Charles Nutter runs a JRuby workshop, Marco Roth delivers "Herb &amp; ReActionView: Mid-2026 Progress Update," and Carmine Paolino argues "Ruby Is the Best Language for Building AI Web Apps," the same case he made in Sofia two weeks earlier.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">May 29–31, 2026 · Vienna, Austria</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/rubyconf-austria-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                See the full lineup
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-[2px] bg-white/15 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-10">
                        <!-- Event: Balkan Ruby -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Balkan Ruby 2026 in Sofia</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 15–16, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">12 talks heavy on AI and Rails internals: Jean Boussier on multiprocessing as the most efficient way to serve Rails apps, Marco Roth on HTML-aware ERB, Vladimir Dementyev (Evil Martians) with "Drop your app/services!", and a PostgreSQL-to-SQLite migration story from production.</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/balkan-ruby-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                See the lineup
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: Brighton Ruby -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Brighton Ruby Returns June 25</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">June 25, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">The long-running single-day UK conference returns with 11 talks: Rachael Wright-Munn's "Your First Open-Source Contribution," David Paluy's "LLM Telemetry as a First-Class Rails Concern" (the same talk that ran at Blue Ridge — LLM telemetry is having a moment), and Brooke Kuhlmann's Hanami + htmx app for e-ink devices.</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/brighton-ruby-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                See the lineup
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Release: Shopify Summer '26 Edition -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-gold-500 text-ink text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink mb-3">Release</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Shopify Summer '26: Horizon Themes, AI Blocks</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Rails Foundation Core member ships 150+ changes: the Horizon theme system with 10 free themes and AI block generation via Shopify Magic, up to 50% faster cart and checkout, a ground-up POS v10, Sidekick answering plain-English questions over ShopifyQL, and Payments in 16 new countries.</p>
                            <a href="https://www.shopify.com/editions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Persona Clears FedRAMP Moderate</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The SF identity unicorn ($2B valuation, Rails backend) earns FedRAMP Moderate Authorization as the only identity-verification provider in the FedRAMP 20x Phase 2 pilot. Federal agencies can now deploy Persona directly via the FedRAMP Marketplace and Carahsoft.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260521233540/en/Persona-Achieves-FedRAMP-Moderate-Authorization-Giving-Federal-Agencies-Modern-Identity-Verification" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit">Funding</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Great Question Raises $13M Series A</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The Bay Area UX research platform (YC W21, Rails + React) raises from Inovia Capital to expand its AI-driven research tools. Customers include ServiceNow, Brex, Canva, and Asana.</p>
                                <a href="https://greatquestion.co/blog/series-a" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-ruby-500 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit">AI + Ruby</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Natural: Agentic Payments, Built on Rails</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The SF startup building payment infrastructure for AI agents (wallets, pay, request, and credit across banking and stablecoins) runs Ruby on Rails under the hood. Out of stealth with a $9.8M seed, and currently hiring 15 engineering roles.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.natural.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 3 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <!-- Press: RubyGems security -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="px-font inline-block px-2 py-1.5 bg-emerald-600 text-white text-[0.5rem] border-2 border-ink w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">RubyGems Repels a Supply-Chain Attack</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Thousands of attacker-controlled accounts flooded the registry with tens of thousands of malicious packages (May 11). RubyGems suspended new signups, yanked 500+ packages, shipped WAF and rate-limiting fixes with Fastly, and reopened registrations within five days. The week the Ruby Alliance launched, its reason to exist made the case in production.</p>
                                <a href="https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/rubygems-suspends-new-signups-after.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Acquisition: Toptal + Adeva -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
